(*"management_resources_schema.assignment_object_relationship"
An **assignment_object_relationship** is a relationship between two objects of the <<express:management_resources_schema.assignment_object_select,assignment_object_select>> list representing the same object in different organizational contexts.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.assignment_object_relationship.description"
the text or the set of texts that provide further information about the **assignment_object_relationship**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.assignment_object_relationship.id"
the identifier or set of identifiers for the **assignment_object_relationship**.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.assignment_object_relationship.related"
the other object of <<express:management_resources_schema.assignment_object_select,assignment_object_select>> that is part of the relationship.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.assignment_object_relationship.relating"
one object of <<express:management_resources_schema.assignment_object_select,assignment_object_select>> that is part of the relationship.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.assignment_object_relationship.relation_type"
the meaning of the relationship.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.assignment_object_relationship.wr:WR1"
An **assignment_object_relationship** shall not participate in its own definition.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.attribute_classification_assignment"
An **attribute_classification_assignment** is an association of a class to an attribute of an existing entity in order to characterize it further. The meaning of the class of the existing attribute is determined by the role.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.attribute_classification_assignment.assigned_class"
the <<express:group_schema.group,group>> that serves as a classification.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.attribute_classification_assignment.attribute_name"
the attribute for which the classification is defined. The **attribute_name** shall identify an attribute of the assigned entity.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.attribute_classification_assignment.role"
the <<express:management_resources_schema.classification_role,classification_role>> that specifies the purpose of the association of the **attribute_classification_assignment** with product data.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.attribute_classification_assignment.role.__note"
The values related to this attribute can be specified in an annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"management_resources_schema.attribute_value_assignment"
An **attribute_value_assignment** is an extendion of the cardinality of a string valued attribute in an entity data type by one. The relationship of the extension to the existing attribute is determined by the role. The entity data types that have the attribute for which the extension is provided are identified by a specialization of <<express:management_resources_schema.attribute_value_assignment,attribute_value_assignment>>.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.attribute_value_assignment.attribute_name"
the attribute for which the additional value is defined. The **attribute_name** shall identify an attribute of the assigned entity.
*)

(*"management_resources_schema.attribute_value_assignment.attribute_name.__example"
'name' and 'description' are examples for the *attribute_name*.
*)

(*"management_resources_schema.attribute_value_assignment.attribute_name.__note"
The identified attribute may be defined in the entity or inherited from a supertype.
*)

(*"management_resources_schema.attribute_value_assignment.attribute_value"
the <<express:management_resources_schema.attribute_type,attribute_type>> that contains, as <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>>, the additional value for the attribute of the assigned entity specified by **attribute_name**.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.attribute_value_assignment.role"
the <<express:management_resources_schema.attribute_value_role,attribute_value_role>> that specifies the purpose of the association of the **attribute_value_assignment** with product data.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.attribute_value_assignment.role.__note"
The values related to this attribute can be specified in an annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"management_resources_schema.attribute_value_assignment.wr:IP1"
The type of **attribute_value** (label or text) shall be the same as the type of the attribute specified by **attribute_name**.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.attribute_value_role"
An **attribute_value_role** is a description of the purpose of an additional value assigned to an attribute of an entity.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.attribute_value_role.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **attribute_value_role**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
