(*"management_resources_schema.acyclic_identification_assignment_relationship"
The **acyclic_identification_assignment_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:management_resources_schema.identification_assignment,identification_assignment>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either an <<express:management_resources_schema.identification_assignment_relationship,identification_assignment_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.acyclic_identification_assignment_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"management_resources_schema.acyclic_identification_assignment_relationship.__note"
This function is not used in this schema. It is defined here because other ISO 10303 integrated resources and application protocols that use the <<express:management_resources_schema.identification_assignment_relationship,identification_assignment_relationship>> entity include rules that use this function.
*)

(*"management_resources_schema.acyclic_identification_assignment_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:management_resources_schema.identification_assignment_relationship,identification_assignment_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.acyclic_identification_assignment_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:management_resources_schema.identification_assignment,identification_assignment>> that the function is searching for in the <<express:management_resources_schema.identification_assignment_relationship.relating_identification_assignment,relating_identification_assignment>> parameter of the relation argument.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.acyclic_identification_assignment_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified entity name of a type of <<express:management_resources_schema.identification_assignment_relationship,identification_assignment_relationship>> entity.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.acyclic_assignment_object_relationship"
The **acyclic_assignment_object_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:management_resources_schema.assignment_object_select,assignment_object_select>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either an <<express:management_resources_schema.assignment_object_relationship,assignment_object_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.acyclic_assignment_object_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"management_resources_schema.acyclic_assignment_object_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:management_resources_schema.assignment_object_relationship,assignment_object_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.acyclic_assignment_object_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:management_resources_schema.assignment_object_select,assignment_object_select>> for which the function is searching in the <<express:management_resources_schema.assignment_object_relationship.relating,relating>> parameter of the relation argument.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.acyclic_assignment_object_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified name of a subtype of the <<express:management_resources_schema.assignment_object_relationship,assignment_object_relationship>> entity.
